# Perception eval images. The labels (data/perception/labels.jsonl) are always
# committed; the photos depend on where they came from.
#
# holdout/ and adversarial/ are personal wardrobe shots and this repo is public,
# so they stay out — see data/perception/README.md for the reproducibility
# tradeoff that implies.
#
# public/ is the exception: every file is CC/PD-licensed from Wikimedia Commons
# and carries its author and licence in the label, so it is redistributable and
# committing it makes that split's numbers reproducible by anyone.
data/perception/images/**
# Re-admit the split directories first — git will not look inside an excluded
# directory, so without this the .gitkeep rule below can never match.
!data/perception/images/*/
!data/perception/images/**/.gitkeep
!data/perception/images/public/**

# Cached VLM replies from the perception eval — reproducible, and they cost money to regenerate.
data/perception/.vlm_cache/
# Cached Jev judgments and text-model replies from the evals, same reasoning.
data/perception/.judge_cache/
evaluation/.cache/

# MCP browser scratch (page snapshots, console logs, upload fixtures)
.playwright-mcp/

# Planning notes stay local (never published)
BACKEND_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md
PERCEPTION_PROGRESS.md
